 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? For training, I' say two or three times week is enough to see improvement without overdoing it. You should be able to talk while you ride and keep your breathing easy. If it feels hard, back off a bit. That's actually make you tired and less fast. Fair guess. Try talking to yourself as the tire deflates. If you can still have a conversation, Lower the pressure a lot in the rain, or just wear gloves. Lower pressures in the rain increase the risk of flats though, so watch your tires closely.",
